      "topic_id": "frustum_volume_surface_area",
      "prompt": "A frustum is formed from a cone with a bottom radius of 8 cm and a top radius of 6 cm, and a vertical height of 9 cm. Find its volume, correct to 1 decimal place.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Full cone height H = R × h ÷ (R - r) = 8 × 9 ÷ (8 - 6) = 36.00 cm (similar triangles)",
        "Big cone volume = (1/3) × π × R² × H, small cone volume = (1/3) × π × r² × (H - h)",
        "Frustum volume = (1/3) × π × h × (R² + Rr + r²) = (1/3) × π × 9 × (8² + 8×6 + 6²)",
        "= 1394.9 cm³ (1 d.p.)"
      ],
      "final_answer": "1394.9 cm³",
      "marks": 5,
      "mark_scheme": [
